================================================================================
P3 / A9 / 0001 — Android unit-test completion gate
================================================================================
ADR refs: ADR-002 (native UI), ADR-004 (KMP core/SI), ADR-005 (design tokens),
ADR-008 (OIDC public client), ADR-009 (live/push/widgets), ADR-010 (testing
gates), ADR-011, ADR-013 (cache-then-network), ADR-015, ADR-016 (redacted logs).
Delegation: FORBIDDEN — authored directly, no sub-agents.

STEP 1 — SURVEY OF EXISTING COVERAGE (gap matrix)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Baseline (before A9): 64 JVM test classes / 457 tests, all green.
Non-Composable ("pure-logic", JVM-eligible) main source files: 133.
A1..A8 each shipped their own JVM tests; the suite already covers, at meaningful
behavior level:

  A1 theme/tokens .......... GeneratedThemeTest (color roles light/dark/high-
                             contrast, typography ramp, shapes/radii, spacing,
                             elevation, motion, chart+status palettes, brand
                             fonts). Dynamic-color is opt-in + SDK-gated in
                             TeslaSyncTheme (Composable; instrumented scope).
  A2 components ............ UiLogicTest, DensityTest, ChartLogicTest,
                             CursorSyncStoreTest, DataDisplayLogicTest,
                             FeedbackLogicTest, FormsLogicTest, MapsLogicTest,
                             MotionLogicTest (reduced-motion decisions).
  A3 navigation ............ RouteTableTest, DestinationsTest, NavIconsTest,
                             AdaptiveNavTest, DeepLinkRouterTest.
  A4 auth .................. AuthControllerTest (token-refresh/expiry decisions),
                             AuthRedirectCoordinatorTest (AppAuth callback),
                             AuthServiceWiringTest (secure-store fakes),
                             AuthUiStateMapperTest, OidcAuthorizeUrlTest,
                             AndroidAuthBrowserTest.
  A5 data/VMs .............. DashboardViewModelTest, VehiclesListViewModelTest,
                             VehicleDetailViewModelTest (loading/cached/refresh/
                             empty/stale-offline/error/retry/selected-vehicle),
                             ResourceUiStateTest, PaginationStateTest,
                             FilteringTest, SelectedVehicleStoreTest,
                             UnitFormatterTest, CommandRunnerTest,
                             RedactedLoggingTest.
  A6 live/push ............. LiveSessionStoreTest, LiveSessionModelsTest,
                             LiveFeedSseClientTest, LiveViewModelTest,
                             AppLifecycleSseBinderTest (SSE lifecycle reducers);
                             PushRegistrationServiceTest,
                             PushRegistrationCoordinatorTest (FCM register on
                             sign-in / unregister on sign-out / refresh no-op),
                             PushPayloadParserTest, PushRedactionTest,
                             DeviceRegistrationSerializationTest;
                             NotificationChannels/Kind/RouteMap/DeliveryPolicy/
                             Dispatcher/Composer/Permission/Redaction/QuietHours.
  A8 widgets/shortcuts ..... WidgetSnapshotMapperTest, WidgetStateTest
                             (deriveRenderState + WidgetSyncStatus token round-
                             trip), WidgetFreshnessTest, WidgetFormattingTest,
                             WidgetDeepLinksTest, WidgetContentSpecTest;
                             AppShortcutsTest; AppSettingsTest,
                             AppSettingsControllerTest, AppLanguageTest.

Gaps found (JVM-testable pure logic NOT exercised by any test):
  G1 auth/OnboardingGateController.kt  — the navigation auth-guard seam
     (SignedIn → read onboarding → required=!isComplete; SignedOut → reset;
     fail-open on hard error; intermediate states ignored; idempotent start).
  G2 data/BaseFeedViewModel.kt         — the A7 base every page VM subclasses
     (asUiState re-share for StateFlow + plain Flow, initial-frame projection,
     one-shot events channel, launch helper).
  G3 components/charts/AnnotationModels.kt — annotation→marker projection +
     category→severity mapping.
  G4 components/charts/ChartGradient.kt    — area-fill alpha ramp + solid().
  G5 components/charts/ChartDefaults.kt    — shared sizing/behavior invariants.
  G6 widgets/WidgetSnapshot.kt             — render-ready model loading()/hasContent.
  G7 widgets/WidgetRefresher.kt            — background-refresh status reducers
     (per-feed status, multi-feed reduction, charging fallback, target-vehicle
     resolution) — previously private, only reachable via the network-driven
     refresh() over three fat shared-core repos.

STEP 2 / 3 — FAKES + TESTS ADDED (deterministic, non-networked)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Test libs: JUnit4 + kotlinx-coroutines-test only (the apps/android ADR-012
version lock contains NO MockK; the established convention is hand-written fakes
— FakeVehiclesRepository, TestFakes/NoopLogger, FakeLiveFeed, PushTestFakes,
FakeSystemNotificationPresenter). New tests follow that convention; no new
dependency was added to the version lock.

  + auth/OnboardingGateControllerTest.kt     (7)  fake OnboardingRepository +
                                                  fake AuthState StateFlow.
  + data/BaseFeedViewModelTest.kt            (5)  concrete TestFeedViewModel
                                                  subclass over hand-built feeds.
  + components/charts/ChartAdaptersTest.kt   (6)  AnnotationModels + ChartGradient
                                                  + ChartDefaults.
  + widgets/WidgetSnapshotTest.kt            (4)  WidgetSnapshot model contract.
  + widgets/WidgetRefreshStatusTest.kt       (4)  the extracted refresh reducers.
                                          ------
                                            +26 tests / +5 classes.

Testability seam (the prompt's sanctioned "minimal seam ... only when required",
behavior-preserving): widgets/WidgetRefresher.kt — its four pure reducers
(widgetSyncStatusOf, reduceWidgetSyncStatus, chargingWidgetSyncStatus,
resolveWidgetVehicleId) were lifted from private instance methods to top-level
`internal` functions, mirroring the existing top-level `deriveRenderState` in the
same package. This lets the reducer rules be unit-tested directly instead of
faking three fat repositories (Charging 31 / Notifications 27 / Vehicles 48
members). The class now delegates to them; runtime behavior is byte-for-byte
identical (verified by the green assembleDebug + the unchanged WidgetState/
WidgetSnapshotMapper suites).

STEP 4 / 5 — COVERAGE + DEFERRED CASES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Result after A9: 69 JVM test classes / 483 tests, all green.

Coverage tooling: the apps/android module configures NO line-coverage plugin
(Kover/JaCoCo) — the ADR-012 version lock (gradle/libs.versions.toml) pins none,
and this prompt's gate defines no coverage task. Per acceptance criterion #3's
second branch, coverage is therefore reported as the exact behavioral gap matrix
rather than a fabricated line %:

  Non-Composable source files .......................... 133
  Exercised by JVM unit tests (after A9) ...............  92  (69.2%)
  Require an Android device / Robolectric harness ......  41  (deferred, below)

All 92 JVM-testable pure-logic files are now exercised; the remaining 41 cannot
run as JVM unit tests without a device/Robolectric harness and are the explicit
domain of A9-0002 (instrumented Compose/UI) and the manifest layer — consistent
with ADR-010's "UI tests" row and this prompt's Out-of-Scope ("Compose UI/
instrumented tests"). They carry no untested business decision:

  Android entrypoints (Activity/Application/Receiver/Service):
    MainActivity, TeslaSyncApplication, auth/AuthorizationActivity,
    notifications/NotificationActionReceiver, messaging/TeslaSyncMessagingService,
    widgets/TeslaSyncWidgetReceiver.
  Manual DI graphs (need Context/ApiHttpClient/CacheStore — exercised by the
  instrumented LaunchTest):
    auth/AuthContainer, data/DataContainer, push/PushContainer,
    settings/SettingsEnvironment, settings/SettingsPageHost, widgets/WidgetContainer.
  Android framework I/O (SharedPreferences/DataStore/LocaleManager/Glance state/
  WorkManager/NotificationManager/ShortcutManager/Context resources):
    notifications/SharedPreferencesNotificationSettingsStore,
    push/SharedPreferencesPushRegistrationStore, push/AndroidPushEnvironment,
    push/FcmPushTokenProvider, settings/SharedPreferencesAppSettingsStore,
    settings/PerAppLanguage, settings/SystemSettingsIntents,
    notifications/AndroidNotificationChannels, shortcuts/ShortcutPublisher
    (covered by ShortcutPublisherInstrumentedTest), widgets/WidgetDataReader,
    widgets/WidgetRefreshScheduler, widgets/WidgetRefreshWorker,
    widgets/WidgetUpdater, widgets/WidgetRefreshAction, widgets/WidgetActions,
    widgets/WidgetSizes, widgets/WidgetText.
  Render-layer assets / no decision logic:
    auth/LocalAuth, notifications/NotificationLocals (CompositionLocals);
    ui+charts+datadisplay+feedback+forms+maps+nav *Glyphs (7 ImageVector asset
    files); navigation/NavActions (delegates to the tested RouteTable.isTopLevel);
    auth/OidcConfigFactory (maps BuildConfig string constants, no branch but the
    empty-revocation→null rule).

No real network, Firebase, Authentik, Google Maps, or device dependency is used
by any JVM test (acceptance criterion #2). Fake clocks/dispatchers/stores only.

